11,464,556,658} carry ~90 events each before and drop to ~0 after; {674,876,1220,1418,1676,1838} are ~0 before and carry ~90 each after (step_03, step_04, step_05, step_06). The transition is sharp (a ~2k-unit gap with 0 events, step_05/step_06).\n- **But the question is about a change of *contacts*, not of active members.** Comparing the partner sets with a 5000 half-window around the candidate change point 43052: pre-window partners of 556/658 (step_13, step_14, step_29) and post-window partners of 876/674 (step_15, step_09) are the *same* 30-node set {150, 204, 207, 224, 230, 262, 487, 640, 788, 823, 913, 916, 992, 1010, 1132, 1165, 1186, 1294, 1308, 1347, 1372, 1520, 1556, 1575, 1590, 1698, 1728, 1798, 1805, 1938}. Jaccard \u2248 0.94 (step_28), the only differences being singleton stray contacts (448, 1700, 1309 \u2014 step_25, step_10, step_24).\n- The same partner set recurs at the far ends of the period too: 327/390/464/411 early (step_16, step_19, step_23, step_27) and 1418/1838/1220/1676 late (step_17, step_18, step_22, step_26). So there is no old-contacts\u2192new-contacts substitution anywhere in [28052, 58052].\n- Confounder checks: the partners are not merely globally popular hubs absorbing everything (each has only 13\u201317 distinct partners and ~37\u201341 events over the full 30k window, step_21); the group members themselves dominate the top-activity list (step_20), so \"recent popularity\" of the contacts does not explain the stable overlap. No triangle/clustering artifact (step_30).\n\n**Conclusion: no regime switch of interaction partners.** The neighbourhood is constant; only which group member speaks to it rotates.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_d9748f02\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [327, 390, 411, 464, 556, 658, 674, 876, 1220, 1418, 1676, 1838],\n  \"window\": [28052, 58052],\n  \"confidence\": 0.82,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_28\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_26\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_29\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_30\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Around t=43052 the group shows a sharp membership handoff (327/390/411/464/556/658 go silent, 674/876/1220/1418/1676/1838 activate), but the set of external contacts is unchanged: the same 30 partners (150,204,207,224,230,262,487,640,788,823,913,916,992,1010,1132,1165,1186,1294,1308,1347,1372,1520,1556,1575,1590,1698,1728,1798,1805,1938) are contacted before and after, Jaccard ~0.94, with only stray singleton differences. No old-contact cohort is replaced by a new one, so the regime-switch signature (abrupt turnover of interaction partners) is absent; the constant partner set is also not explained by hub popularity, since those partners have low overall degree in the window.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 97861, "total_output_tokens": 9981, "total_tokens": 107842, "total_latency_ms": 143338, "llm_calls": 14, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}